\f0\fs24 \cf0 # ReservoirX-D\
\
Generate directed, degree-regular reservoir weight matrices \'97 and test whether that wiring actually helps on your configuration, instead of taking it on faith.\
\
FastAPI service. No database required. Deterministic given a seed. 59 tests.\
\
---\
\
## Why this is not just a matrix generator\
\
The regular-degree connectivity thesis has mixed support across architectures. A sparse CNN showed a real effect. A mixture-of-experts transformer showed none. The reservoir result the service is named after came from an external pipeline that the benchmark capsule never reproduced.\
\
So ReservoirX-D ships the experiment rather than the conclusion:\
\
- `POST /compare` runs regular-vs-skewed on **your** parameters \'97 paired by seed, matched on edge budget, Holm-corrected across tasks, with an optional symmetrisation control that *measures* whether directedness matters rather than estimating it from a structural proxy.\
- `POST /optimize` selects a width on one set of seeds and confirms it on a set never used for selection. Connection savings are counted from the generated graphs.\
- `GET /claims` returns the evidential status of every claim behind the service, including the two marked `external_unverified`.\
\
If the effect isn't there on your configuration, the API tells you so.\
\
